{
  "id": "RLSA-2026:83157",
  "title": "Important: kernel security, bug fix, and enhancement update",
  "issued": {
    "date": "2026-10-16 12:01:11"
  },
  "updated": {
    "date": "2026-10-17 00:15:36"
  },
  "severity": "Important",
  "description": "The kernel packages contain the Linux kernel, the core of any Linux operating system.\n\nSecurity Fix(es):\n\n* kernel: Linux kernel: Denial of Service due to use-after-free in act_tunnel_key (CVE-2026-68377)\n\n* kernel: ASoC: SOF: ipc3-control: Fix heap overflow in bytes_ext put/get (CVE-2026-72262)\n\n* kernel: net/sched: cls_route: fix fastmap use-after-free on filter (CVE-2026-74583)\n\n* kernel: ALSA: usx2y: bound the hwdep mmap fault offset (CVE-2026-74641)\n\n* kernel: udp: fix potential use-after-free in tunnel segmentation (CVE-2026-74705)\n\n* kernel: svcrdma: Validate Read chunk positions before reconstruction (CVE-2026-89526)\n\n* kernel: NFSD: Prevent client use-after-free during blocked-lock reaping (CVE-2026-90036)\n\n* kernel: svcrdma: Reject Write/Reply chunks with segcount 0 (CVE-2026-93228)\n\n* kernel: md/raid5-ppl: fix use-after-free in ppl_do_flush() (CVE-2026-93262)\n\nBug Fix(es) and Enhancement(s):\n\n* powerpc/pseries: pci - logic bug in SR-IOV enable (JIRA:Rocky Linux-240146)\n\nFor more details about the security issue(s), including the impact, a CVSS score, acknowledgments, and other related information, refer to the CVE page(s) listed in the References section.",
